      "writtenOn": "2024-02-12T14:55:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "getNamesForUids can do some weird things: https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/ComputerEngine.java;drc\u003dc3296a0c1a1e72b672aa4fbf516de4f342df42b2;l\u003d4414\nIt could return an empty string if it doesn\u0027t recognise the UID.\nIt could return \"shared:\" plus a shared user name (which need not be a package name) if the UID is shared by multiple packages. (Which is deprecated, but still a thing.)\nI\u0027m not entirely sure what will happen if the UID is in different user to user 0.\n\nAnd we should probably special case uid 0, or perhaps any non-app UID.\n\n\nTBH I\u0027m not sure we should be looking at package names at all.\n\nAlthough I know @ioffe@google.com made a good case for doing so.",
